      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_4e244322a79c29526d38339c1bba355cb25e8ff727749be703030366888be43d",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The proof architecture separates a net signed statistic into one-sided masses and controls the unwanted side by comparison with a better-understood zero population. This turns cancellation-prone global information into a directional conclusion.",
